Executive verdict
Ready for a controlled beta/showcase, with one flagged security item to close first. The auth incident that could have embarrassed a live demo (site-wide 403 on login) has been root-caused, fixed, migration-tracked, and verified live against the real project ref tlavrxiaegbtyfmjfdcz. That's exactly the kind of fix you want closed before showing this to others.

What's verified solid
Repo health: 549 commits, 7 branches, live Vercel deploy linked directly in the repo "About" section, AGPL-3.0 license, contributing guide, security policy, and code of conduct all present.

Auth root cause, fixed properly: the site-wide login 403 was two permissive SELECT policies on public.users being OR'd together, where the second policy called is_admin() — and authenticated had never been granted EXECUTE on it, so the whole query died with Postgres error 42501 before reaching the correct "own row" policy. That's now migration-tracked (20260724182817_grant_is_admin_execute.sql), so it can't silently regress on a future schema reset.

Password reset, closed end-to-end: ForgotPassword + ResetPassword built into Auth.tsx, routes wired in App.tsx, and live-verified against the real project — real recovery email, real link, landed signed-in on /reset-password, password updated, redirected to /dashboard. Expired-link state and duplicate-password rejection were also tested.

Signup 500, root-caused and recurrence-protected: public.users had a UNIQUE(email) with no FK back to auth.users, so deleted auth accounts left permanent orphan rows blocking that email from ever signing up again. Four live orphans found (including the exact blocked address), zero dependent data confirmed before deletion, and an ON DELETE CASCADE FK added so this class of bug can't recur.

Discipline shown: get_or_create_referral_code() had the identical missing-grant symptom, but the team correctly refused to blanket-grant it because it takes an arbitrary user_id with no caller check — that would've been a privilege-escalation hole. It's explicitly logged as its own follow-up task, not folded into the auth batch.

Front-end product loop: live homepage clearly sells the mission, shows free-start friction removal ("Try Level 1 free — no signup", "No credit card"), and visibly ties Courses → Vibe Labs → Pets → Shop → BROski$ into one loop.

BROskiPets sister repo: active within hours, deep folder structure (contracts, frontend, shop, rewards, tests, docs), and its own operating docs (CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md, TRUTH.md).

