2. /admin/mission-control force-signs the user out
Visiting that route (linked publicly from the footer's "weird" word on every single page) shows "Checking access..." then silently logs the user out and dumps them on the logged-out homepage — no error message, no permission-denied state. Reproduced twice, consistent. Two issues in one: an access-denied path should never blow away a valid session, and a route named /admin/... shouldn't be linked from public footer copy at all.

3. Referral button is dead
On /tokens, "Refer a friend — earn 100 BROski$" does nothing when clicked — no link generated, no copy action, no toast, just a performance warning in devtools ("Event handlers... blocked UI updates for 202ms"). This lines up exactly with the known open get_or_create_referral_code() 403 issue Claude flagged — good that it's already tracked, but worth knowing it's user-facing and clickable right now, which will look broken to anyone testing it.

